---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import portrait from "../assets/deep-sherchan.png";

const title = "Ex-Tech Startup Founder - Deep Sherchan";
const description =
	"Born in Nepal. Started a company in India, later sold it to a US company. Currently in Australia, learning to be a father and a husband.";
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
	<div class="container mx-auto py-4 px-4 grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
		<figure>
			<Image
				class="mx-auto rounded-md border"
				src={portrait}
				width={550}
				height={553}
				format="webp"
				alt="Deep Sherchan"
			/>
		</figure>
		<div>
			<article class="prose prose-a:text-primary">
				<h1>Ex-Tech Startup Founder</h1>

				<div class="text-sm italic">
					...Born in Nepal. Started a company in India, later sold it to a US
					company. Currently in Australia, learning to be a father and a husband.
				</div>
				<p>
					In mid-2008, I packed my bags and left Nepal to experiment with my
					life. I still haven't found my way back. Like Siddhartha in Hermann
					Hesse's novel, I am still seeking...
				</p>
				<p>
					I still remember my five-day journey from Kathmandu to Bangalore, the
					Silicon Valley of Asia, by bus, jeep and train. On the first day, I saw
					a big poster that read, "Bangalore's official language is C." The logos
					of every global technology company rose in the distance, like the
					mountains of the Kathmandu Valley.
				</p>
				<p>
					Everything I know about running a tech business comes from my decade in
					Bangalore: my friends, colleagues and clients. I will never forget
					running to my friend's apartment at 2 a.m. to take a client call from
					the US because the lights had gone out in mine. Growing a company from
					nothing and battling the day-to-day demands of clients was a
					life-changing experience. Over the years, I watched the jobs I once did
					alone become whole teams, each with its own processes. Eventually, I
					stepped away and handed it over.
				</p>
				<p>
					With all that knowledge and experience, I landed in Australia in
					mid-2018, this time by plane only. Looking out the window, I took in
					Australia's unassuming landscape as we landed at Tullamarine Airport in
					Melbourne. A few weeks later, my wife and I drove 11 hours in a Hyundai
					Getz to Adelaide, South Australia, which I now call home. Here, I have
					become a father and a husband...
				</p>
			</article>
		</div>
	</div>
</BaseLayout>
